// @check
// @error unknown type 'nope' within '{foo:string}|{[string]:nope}'
// @error print of () -> <error> is type-valid but not yet supported by codegen
// CONTRACT (must-error): an UNRESOLVED MAP VALUE type is reported. `mkMapTy(string, -1)`
// is indistinguishable from the empty-`Map()` inference hole, so the annotation read as
// "value type not yet known" rather than "no such type": the checker accepted it and the
// emitter produced a module that fails to parse as WebAssembly.
//
// The SECOND error is not a cascade of the first: `print(f)` passes the FUNCTION VALUE
// itself, whose rep is a WasmGC reference the scalar print imports cannot take — it is
// rejected for the same reason `closures/print-closure-rejected.vl` is, and would be
// rejected identically if the return annotation resolved. Only the RENDER of the return
// type (`<error>`) comes from the first error. This file is the one pre-existing corpus
// cell the `print(<reference>)` gate uncovered.
function f(): {foo: string} | {[string]: nope} { return { foo: "a" } }
print(0)
print(f)
